    "text": {
     "en": "The story shows that freedom is more valuable than comfort. The parrot had fruits and a golden cage, but it still wanted the sky.\nIt also shows that intelligence can be more useful than strength.\nThe parrot did not argue. It used a clever plan. The wild parrot's fall taught it how to escape.\nThe merchant's love was real but selfish, because he wanted to keep the bird with him.\nThink: if you were the merchant how would you respond? Which parrot was truly wise?\n(additional, not in the textbook) Real love respects another's freedom."
    }
